+4. **Keybag relay.** after xART storage and NCM readiness, `sep-probe` checks
+   for the live biometric keybag. An existing unlocked bag must accept the saved
+   secret and pass a lock-state readback; it is not reloaded or re-promoted at
+   every authentication handoff. Only an explicit not-found response restores
+   the saved bag, observes the promoted bag, resolves its protected-user binding,
+   and publishes first-unlock. Both paths initialize ACM, confirm the final
+   biometric device state, and hold the notification relay. The service is pulled
+   in by the ready xART instance rather than
